	)
	(text "SAFETY-CRITICAL: HEAT ENABLE CHARGE PUMP  (HR-07 / SR-02 / AD-05)\nHEAT_EN must be TOGGLED by the safety task (~5 Hz) to hold the contactor closed.\nA static HIGH level CANNOT hold it -- do not \"simplify\" this to a plain GPIO drive.\nC23=10uF pump, R19=100R limit, D5=BAT54S, C24=3.3uF store, R20=47k bleed + gate pulldown.\nHolds ~2.5 V at Q3 gate; if toggling stops the coil releases in ~0.15 s (NFR-04 allows 1 s)."
		(at 181.864 183.388 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "7ca3ae12-7d98-418c-b85f-3dd3c7ecdd90")
	)
	(text "KNOWN ACCEPTED ERC VIOLATION: U3.SDO and U4.SDO both sit on SPI_MISO.\nThe KiCad symbol types these pins \"output\", but the MAX31856 tri-states SDO\nwhenever its CS is de-asserted, so the shared bus is correct. Separate CS lines\n(TC1_CS / TC2_CS) guarantee only one device drives at a time. Exclude in ERC."
		(at 456.184 27.178 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "8a0be164-57e9-4df8-8916-7b4e7db1e202")
	)
	(text "POWER"
		(at 22.606 24.384 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(thickness 0.508)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "a4f70b81-f8a4-432f-89b5-dfe3aa4171ce")
	)
